From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Another area's palettes written straight into their bank
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 0100 loaded another area's texture palettes with NNS_G3dPlttLoad,
which takes the palette bank off the 3D while it copies (GX_BeginLoadTexPltt)
and puts it back: the game does that at its map changes, but these are
loaded in play, as a map of the other area first comes into the view, and
the 3D's thread reads the banks on its own, so a scene could be drawn with
no palettes for a moment. They're now written straight into the bank as
it's mapped (NitroPort_WriteTexPltt), NNS_G3dPlttLoad only where a slot has
no bank. On the PC from Route 209 the same pictures.

---
diff --git a/src/overlay005/land_data.c b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
index 3fa8d31f..15a28ffb 100644
--- a/src/overlay005/land_data.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
@@ -3113,9 +3113,19 @@ static BOOL Port_LoadExtraTextures(NNSG3dResTex *tex, u32 base, u32 *at, NNSG3dP
     }
 
     if (plttSize > 0) {
+        // (straight into the palette bank as mapped: NNS_G3dPlttLoad takes
+        // the bank off the 3D while it loads, and the 3D's thread reads it
+        // on its own; the game's own loads are at its map changes)
+        extern int NitroPort_WriteTexPltt(u32 addr, const void *src, u32 size);
+
         NNS_G3dPlttSetPlttKey(tex, *plttKey);
-        DC_FlushRange(tex, tex->header.size);
-        NNS_G3dPlttLoad(tex, TRUE);
+
+        if (NitroPort_WriteTexPltt(NNS_GfdGetPlttKeyAddr(*plttKey), NNS_G3dGetPlttData(tex), (u32)tex->plttInfo.sizePltt << 3)) {
+            tex->plttInfo.flag |= NNS_G3D_RESPLTT_LOADED;
+        } else {
+            DC_FlushRange(tex, tex->header.size);
+            NNS_G3dPlttLoad(tex, TRUE);
+        }
     }
 
     return TRUE;
